A||N||5||GT-maniac||E-Brake question||||9||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||06-01-2000||06:19 PM||||Hi all, anyone ever had to replace they're emergency brake cables ? I've got all the cables in but somethings wrong. According to the Haynes manual the e-brake arms should be against the stops on the brake assembly with the adjuster nut loosened all the way. Well when they're in that position the threaded rod that's part of the left brake cable doesn't even reach the adjuster nut. It's a good half an inch away. Now I can force the rod and the nut to tie together but then the left brake is on so tightly the wheel won't move. Have I just got the wrong cable for the left wheel or is there something else I'm missing here ?<P>thanks in advance ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-01-2000||11:25 PM||||That happened to me when I rebuilt my rear calipers, but I was reinstalling the original cables!<BR>This was years ago and all I remember (other than total frustration) is it had something to do with the lever asembly and the piston.<BR>Same as your Fiero, make it fit and one side would drag all the time.<BR>This is good, too much coincidence for it not to have happened to others, and possibly even recently enough to be remembered in detail.<P>Just a long winded way to get this back to the top of the tech forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||DiggityDan||06-02-2000||12:03 AM||||If I remember correctly, there is a recall on certain model Fieros and Trans ams. I would check your VIN against your dealers information to see if your car needs the recall performed. It had something to do with the parking brake cables and actuators.<BR>Just a thought||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-02-2000||01:54 PM||||my Pontiac dealer put new ones on for me parts and labor under the recall. Free. Dont know if that applies though if youve already worked on it. Worth a try if you make sure you keep the old ones and your VIN number is on the list.<P>RG<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||06-02-2000||03:33 PM||||I rebuilt my leaking rear calipers, and took it to the dealer because they still leaked.  Dealer fixed it under the recall, even though I had worked on it.  Turned out the leaking pistons were one of the reasons for the recall, along with the e-brake cables.<BR>Dealer replaced everything free of charge.  <P>Recall # 86-C-16.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT-maniac||06-02-2000||03:59 PM||||Thanks to everyone who replied. Turns out my problems are related to a missing spring on one wheel and screwed up hand brake lever. Hopefully once I get these things my problem will be fixed. Along the way I found out my<BR>car has had all the recall work done on it. ||||reg||1
